  "job": "Raises a dome no enemy can step into, so the ally who got caught has three safe seconds.",
  "difficulty": 1,
  "lore": "Marund raised half the drum walls of the Lamp Dome with his own maul, and he still tests a finished course by knocking on it. Serenade masons say a dome is not done until someone has sheltered under it, so he brings the habit into every fight: he finds whoever is most frightened and builds the evening around them. He speaks slowly, laughs at his own jokes before he reaches the end of them, and has never let an Aubade runner past a wall he set. The stopped evening suits him. There is always time to lay one more course.",
